<webscript>
    <shortname>beCPG Portal: wizard configuration</shortname>
    <description>
        Returns the supplier wizard structure and, for every step, the field definition
        resolved by Share (formId + entityType + siteId + list cascade, client overrides
        included) enriched by the repository form service.

        Consumed by the React supplier portal, which holds an Alfresco ticket and cannot
        run the Share resolution cascade itself.

        Additive endpoint: the Share wizard page (wizard-mgr) is untouched.
    </description>
    <url>/becpg/portal/wizard?wizardId={wizardId}</url>
    <url>/becpg/portal/wizard?wizardId={wizardId}&amp;nodeRef={nodeRef?}&amp;entityType={entityType?}&amp;siteId={siteId?}&amp;mode={mode?}&amp;withItemForm={withItemForm?}</url>
    <format default="json"></format>
    <!--
        An identity is required. The default is `none`, under which the wizard structure -
        its steps, their form ids and their list ids - was readable by anyone.

        `user` is what the caller can satisfy: the portal opens a real Share session
        (POST /share/noauth/becpg/portal/session) and sends its cookie. It used to hold an
        Alfresco ticket only, which is why an earlier attempt kept `none` and checked the
        identity in the script; that premise is gone, and so is the `portalTicket` argument
        this endpoint accepted - a credential in a query string, written to the access log
        of every hop and to browser history.
    -->
    <authentication>user</authentication>
</webscript>
